      "text": [
        ": قُلْتُ لَهُ مَا تَقُولُ فِي رَجُلٍ اِدَّعَى أَنَّهُ خَطَبَ اِمْرَأَةً إِلَى نَفْسِهَا وَ مَازَحَ فَزَوَّجَتْهُ مِنْ نَفْسِهَا وَ هِيَ مَازِحَةٌ فَسُئِلَتِ اَلْمَرْأَةُ عَنْ ذَلِكَ فَقَالَتْ نَعَمْ قَالَ \"لَيْسَ بِشَيْءٍ\" قُلْتُ فَيَحِلُّ لِلرَّجُلِ أَنْ يَتَزَوَّجَهَا قَالَ \"نَعَمْ\"."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.4486 - Al-Bazanti narrated from Al-Mashriqi, who said:\nI asked Abu Al-Hasan (as): What do you say about a man who claimed that he proposed to a woman, and jokingly, she married herself to him while also joking? Then the woman was asked about this, and she said: \"Yes.\"\nImam (as) said: \"It is nothing.\"\nI asked: Is it permissible for the man to marry her?\nImam (as) said: \"Yes.\""
        ]
      }
